{"id": "EUVD-2026-101222", "enisaUuid": "72e07a55-e117-3b2d-b5ae-8d4e0a714296", "description": "BottleCRM 0.43 through 1.14.5 contains a regular expression denial of service vulnerability that allows authenticated organization administrators to block web workers via unbounded routing rule regex patterns. Attackers can create a routing rule with a catastrophically backtracking pattern evaluated by _match_condition() during case saves, exhausting workers shared across all tenants.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T14:16:38", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T11:39:00", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:H/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/Django-CRM/Django-CRM/issues/830", "https://github.com/Django-CRM/Django-CRM/blob/v1.14.5/backend/cases/routing.py#L107-L114", "https://github.com/aaronamran/CVE-Disclosures/tree/main/CVE-2026/CVE-2026-110594", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/bottlecrm-0.43-through-1.14.5-redos-via-case-routing-rule-regex"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-110594", "GHSA-r225-9m2h-4x6v"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.64, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "e2dd90df-5769-3efe-a5d9-5caf36803278", "product": {"name": "BottleCRM", "vendor": {"name": "MicroPyramid"}}, "product_version": "0.43 \u22641.14.5"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "a282a85f-c8aa-3096-bc56-d0843991bd91", "vendor": {"name": "MicroPyramid"}}], "isExploited": false}